# Pinned ref of github.com/monaccode/astromesh built into the Phase 0 image.
# Bump deliberately; CI fails if it cannot resolve this ref.
# v0.28.7: latest release = v0.28.6 mainline + the Fase 4 OTel/metrics/egress runtime
# work (previously only on the unmerged develop branch at 4a9b2283).
# v0.28.9: bump to latest release — adds Moonshot/Kimi (kimi-k2.5/k2.6) OpenAI-compat
# provider support, provider-label cost attribution (v0.28.8) and cache-aware Kimi
# pricing incl. cache_read_input_tokens (v0.28.9). Tag resolvable on origin.
# v0.29.0: transversal per-role model routing — one ModelRouter per orchestration
# role (reasoner/planner/worker/synthesizer/supervisor), undefined roles fall back
# to `default`; source-aware candidate builder + LiteLLM-backed provider (optional
# `litellm` extra) for 100+ cloud models. Tag resolvable on origin.
# v0.34.0: WebSocket wired to the runtime, streaming live run events (tool calls and text)
# over /v1/ws/agent/{name}. Verified before bumping: the .deb resolves under pip, and the
# release keeps v0.33.1's lazy imports plus tests/test_slim_install.py, which guards the
# boot path against a numpy/aiosqlite regression. Tag resolvable on origin.
# v0.33.1: v0.33.0 built a .deb that would not boot — astromesh.api.main imported
# numpy (via the new rag/factory.py -> faiss_store) and aiosqlite (via workflow/store),
# neither of which ships in the image venv, so astromeshd died on ModuleNotFoundError
# and never served /v1/health. Caught by this repo's boot gate. v0.33.1 makes both
# imports lazy. Every release from v0.30.0 to v0.33.0 is unbootable for this reason.
# v0.33.0: core OTLP export is finally wired — setup_observability() builds the
# TelemetryManager/OTLPCollector/MetricsManager from AgentRuntime.bootstrap() under
# ASTROMESH_OTLP_ENABLED (the classes existed but were never instantiated), and the
# node's hand-rolled duplicate wiring is gone. Also Orbit v0.3.0/v0.4.0 (not built
# into the image). Tag resolvable on origin.
#
# NOTE: v0.31.0 and v0.32.0 are deliberately skipped — both are unbuildable here.
# They declare a hard `astromesh-nebula` dependency resolved through a uv source at
# `../../astromesh-nebula`, a sibling repo that is neither checked out on the runner
# nor published on PyPI; build-deb.sh uses pip, which ignores [tool.uv.sources], so
# the .deb build dies on "No matching distribution found for astromesh-nebula".
# v0.33.0 carries the fix (77bc29f) that makes nebula optional.
ASTROMESH_REF=v0.34.0
